                                    <h1>Indian Wedding Season Marketing Playbook for D2C 2026-2027</h1>
                                    <p>Indian wedding season drives massive concentrated revenue for jewelry (40-60% of annual sales), fashion (30-45%), gifting (25-40%), and home + décor D2C brands. Two peak periods: November-February (auspicious month concentration) + April-June (summer weddings + North Indian tradition). Here is the complete playbook.</p>
                                    <h2>Wedding Season Timeline</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Winter wedding season (Nov-Feb):</strong> auspicious months per Hindu calendar concentrate. Peak wedding count.<br><strong>Summer wedding season (April-June):</strong> North Indian summer weddings + destination weddings.<br><strong>Total peak periods:</strong> ~6 months of concentrated wedding activity.<br><strong>Off-peak months (July-Oct):</strong> engagement + planning + shopping preparation.</p>
                                    <h2>Category-Specific Wedding Playbook</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Jewelry:</strong> 40-60% of annual revenue concentrated in wedding season. Bridal jewelry + gifting jewelry + engagement rings + gold coins peak.<br><strong>Ethnic fashion:</strong> bridal lehenga + sherwani + sangeet + reception outfits. 4-6 outfits per wedding across bride + immediate family.<br><strong>Home + décor:</strong> new-home setup (post-wedding) + wedding gift categories.<br><strong>Gifting:</strong> wedding gift market — corporate + personal.<br><strong>Beauty:</strong> bridal makeup + trial services + wedding-day kits.<br><strong>F&amp;B:</strong> wedding hampers + specialty catering.<br><strong>Photography + video:</strong> wedding-adjacent services.</p>
                                    <h2>Planning + Content Timeline</h2>
                                    <p><strong>4-6 months before wedding season:</strong> creative shoots + inventory + creator + wedding-influencer commitments.<br><strong>2-3 months before:</strong> pre-season teaser campaigns.<br><strong>1-2 months before:</strong> full campaign launch.<br><strong>During season:</strong> weekly campaign refreshes + wedding-specific content series.<br>Wedding content is high-consideration — buyers plan 3-6 months ahead. Long consideration windows require sustained content presence.</p>
                                    <h2>The Wedding Buyer Journey</h2>
                                    <p>Bride / groom + parents + close family are all decision makers. Multi-stakeholder purchase requires multi-persona content:<br><strong>Bride content:</strong> Instagram + Pinterest inspiration.<br><strong>Parent content:</strong> family + tradition storytelling.<br><strong>Groom content:</strong> increasingly own category (sherwani + accessories + skincare).<br><strong>Corporate wedding client:</strong> gifting hamper catalogs + volume pricing.</p>
                                    <h2>Ad Budget Concentration</h2>
                                    <p>Wedding season CPM inflation in India: 30-60% during peak months. Concentrate spend during actual purchase decision windows.<br><strong>Recommended allocation:</strong> pre-season teaser (2-3 months out): 10-15%. Peak season (Nov-Feb + April-June): 60-70%. Off-peak retention + planning content: 15-25%.<br>Wedding buyers convert on brand + trust + design + reviews — not price. Discount-heavy wedding marketing loses to brand-heavy.</p>
                                    <h2>Regional Wedding Nuances</h2>
                                    <p><strong>North Indian weddings:</strong> more elaborate + longer + higher gifting spend.<br><strong>South Indian weddings:</strong> silk + gold + traditional-focused.<br><strong>Bengali weddings:</strong> distinctive attire + jewelry styles.<br><strong>Punjabi + Sikh weddings:</strong> vibrant + colorful + music-heavy.<br><strong>Gujarati + Marwari weddings:</strong> heavy jewelry + traditional.<br><strong>Destination weddings:</strong> Goa + Rajasthan + Kerala + Udaipur venues drive tourism-adjacent bookings.<br>Regional-specific creative outperforms generic pan-India wedding content.</p>

